properties-cpp is header only and isn't packaged for arch, so the three headers get
copied into the tree's own include dir in prepare() and the pkg-config check goes away.

the test suite wants gtest, libdbustest and python dbusmock, none of which we build
against, so the subdir only gets pulled in when BUILD_TESTING is asked for.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -48,7 +48,6 @@
                    libedataserver-1.2>=3.5
                    gstreamer-1.0>=1.2
                    libnotify>=0.7.6
-                   properties-cpp>=0.0.1
                    libaccounts-glib>=1.18
                    messaging-menu>=12.10
                    uuid>=2.25)
@@ -82,7 +81,9 @@
 add_subdirectory(src)
 add_subdirectory(data)
 add_subdirectory(po)
-add_subdirectory(tests)
+if (BUILD_TESTING)
+  add_subdirectory(tests)
+endif ()

 # testing & coverage
 find_package(CoverageReport)
